module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.RankOneRootInterfaces
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.ReductiveBorelPairStructure
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.ReductiveRootSubgroupParametrizations
import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.SchemeTangentSpace
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.TrivialTorusCoherentWeightDecomposition
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.ReductiveRankOneReflections
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.TorusPositiveRaySubgroup
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.MultiplicativeTypeLargestSubtorus

/-! # Root generation of an overgroup of a maximal torus

Source: Milne, Algebraic Groups (2017), paragraph 21.66, printed p.444,
using Theorem 21.11(c) and Corollary 10.17
(blueprint: lem-sfb-maximal-torus-overgroup-root-generation).

The root set and weight spaces are the recorded character weights. Both actions
are pinned to conjugation. Every inclusion is a factorization of group-scheme
morphisms, so it holds on points over every commutative F-algebra. The subgroup
in the minimality assertion need not be smooth or connected.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory
open scoped MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RankOneRoots

/-- A smooth connected closed overgroup of a split maximal torus contains precisely
its Lie-theoretic root groups and is generated by them together with that torus.
The family U consists of the smooth connected normalized root subgroups supplied
by lem-sfb-reductive-root-subgroup-parametrizations; hU specifies their tangent spaces.
Source: Milne, paragraph 21.66, printed p.444, using 21.11(c) and 10.17
(blueprint: lem-sfb-maximal-torus-overgroup-root-generation).

Proof plan, following the node:
1. Since jT factors iT through H, conjugation by T preserves H on every test
   algebra. The tangent inclusion is injective and equivariant and contains Lie(T).
   Use def-sc-scheme-tangent-space and lem-sfb-affine-group-lie-tangent-calculus.
   As a closed subscheme of an affine finite-type scheme, H is affine of finite type.
2. Apply lem-sfb-trivial-torus-coherent-weight-decomposition over Spec F.
   By lem-sfb-reductive-rank-one-reflections, the zero weight in Lie(G) is Lie(T)
   and every nonzero root weight is a line. Thus Lie(H) is Lie(T) plus the direct
   sum of exactly the nonzero character weight spaces occurring in Lie(H).
   These are characters, not their differentials, in every characteristic.
3. For a root alpha, reducedness from lem-sfb-reductive-rank-one-reflections
   identifies its positive-ray space with its root line. Apply
   lem-sfb-torus-positive-ray-subgroup to the conjugation action and K = H.
   Its containment implication and the uniqueness assertion of
   lem-sfb-reductive-root-subgroup-parametrizations give U_alpha contained in H
   when the H-weight space is nonzero. Conversely, a factorization through H
   puts the nonzero root tangent line in Lie(H), so that weight space is nonzero.
4. Given J containing the specified generators, form K = H times_G J. It is a
   closed subgroup of H; its points are the intersection of the two subgroups
   on every test algebra. The torus and each selected root group factor through K.
   They are smooth connected by lem-sfb-multiplicative-type-largest-subtorus and
   lem-sfb-reductive-root-subgroup-parametrizations. Their tangent spaces span
   Lie(H) by step 2. Apply lem-sfb-smooth-subgroup-tangent-generation with ambient
   H and containing subgroup K, without assuming smoothness or connectedness of K.
   It gives K = H, hence the group-scheme factorization H into J.
5. Step 3 supplies containment of the generators in H; step 4 supplies minimality.
   If no root occurs in H, the generating family still contains T, and step 2
   gives Lie(H) = Lie(T). This also covers an empty ambient root set and rank zero.
   Evaluation of the factorizations gives the assertions on all algebra points. -/
theorem maximal_torus_overgroup_root_generation
    {F : Type u} [Field F] [IsAlgClosed F]
    (G T : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F))))
    (hG : ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsReductive G)
    (iT : T ⟶ G) (hT : ReductiveTorusCentralizer.IsMaximalTorus iT)
    (hsplit : ∃ r : ℕ, Nonempty (T ≅ MultiplicativeType.splitTorus F r))
    (aG : ModObj T.X G.X) (haG : aG.smul = adjointMap iT)
    (U : roots T G aG → Grp (Over (Spec (.of F))))
    (iU : ∀ α : roots T G aG, U α ⟶ G)
    (hU : ∀ α : roots T G aG,
      IsClosedSubgroupScheme (iU α).hom.hom ∧ Smooth (U α).X.hom ∧
      ConnectedSpace (U α).X.left ∧ @TorusCharacterTangent.IsStable F _ T G aG _ (iU α) ∧
      (GrpObj.differential (iU α).hom.hom).toLinearMap.range = weight T G aG α.val)
    (H : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iH : H ⟶ G)
    (hHclosed : IsClosedSubgroupScheme iH.hom.hom)
    (hHsmooth : Smooth H.X.hom) (hHconn : ConnectedSpace H.X.left)
    (jT : T ⟶ H) (hjT : jT ≫ iH = iT)
    (aH : ModObj T.X H.X) (haH : aH.smul = adjointMap jT) :
    (∀ α : roots T G aG,
      (∃ f : U α ⟶ H, f ≫ iH = iU α) ↔ weight T H aH α.val ≠ ⊥) ∧
    ∀ (J : Grp (Over (Spec (.of F)))) (iJ : J ⟶ G),
      IsClosedSubgroupScheme iJ.hom.hom →
      (∃ f : T ⟶ J, f ≫ iJ = iT) →
      (∀ α : roots T G aG, weight T H aH α.val ≠ ⊥ →
        ∃ f : U α ⟶ J, f ≫ iJ = iU α) →
      ∃ f : H ⟶ J, f ≫ iJ = iH := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.RankOneRoots
